{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 13, :comments ["<b>I will surely deal well.</b> 'I will deal well' — by your merit; 'surely deal well' — by the merit of your fathers (Bereshit Rabbah)." "<b>And I will set your seed as the sand of the sea.</b> And where did He say so to him? For did He not say to him only ״וְהָיָה זַרְעֲךָ כַּעֲפַר הָאָרֶץ״ (Genesis 28)? Rather, He said to him ״כִּי לֹא אֶעֱזָבְךָ עַד אֲשֶׁר אִם עָשִׂיתִי אֵת אֲשֶׁר דִּבַּרְתִּי לָךְ״ (ibid.) — and to Avraham He said ״וְהַרְבָּה אַרְבֶּה אֶת זַרְעֲךָ כְּכוֹכְבֵי הַשָּׁמַיִם וְכַחוֹל אֲשֶׁר עַל שְׂפַת הַיָּם״."], :book :genesis, :voice :rashi, :lang :en, :chapter 32, :notes {}, :source-witnesses nil, :timestamp "2026-08-02T09:01:44.530370922Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}